00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:04.000
Milton Friedman famously said you cannot simultaneously have free immigration

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:07.580
and a welfare state. Economist Brian Caplan begs to differ.

00:00:07.580 --> 00:00:12.240
Caplan makes his case in his latest book,
"Open Borders The Science and Ethics of Immigration."

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:15.480
It's a graphic novel he co-produced with artist Zach Weinersmith,

00:00:15.480 --> 00:00:19.220
who's best known as the creator of the popular web comic, "Saturday Morning Breakfast Cereal."

00:00:19.220 --> 00:00:24.180
The book takes on all the arguments against open borders one by one. From concerns about assimilation,

00:00:24.180 --> 00:00:29.480
terrorism, and fairness, to Friedman's oft-quoted libertarian objection. Caplan sat down with us

00:00:29.480 --> 00:00:33.980
to talk about why immigration works, if he thinks he'll see open borders in his lifetime,

00:00:33.980 --> 00:00:36.220
and why he likes to pick fights in his books.

00:00:38.920 --> 00:00:42.899
